From 3e9dfa5cc8008a596f58d963574a300220c7a478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:14:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 107/119] fix: lit particles were missing the diffuse 1/PI, and
 had been since S2

Particles do not go through TiledForwardShading. They have their own CPU-built
light list, their own accumulator and their own evaluation in LightVolumes.cfi,
and that evaluation does not call anything named *BRDF - which is exactly why the
S2 pi audit walked past it. It listed the particle sun SPECULAR as corrected,
because that one calls BlinnBRDF and was given the factor by hand, and it never
looked at the diffuse half sitting two functions away.

The inputs to that half are the radiometric sun (S2 stopped dividing CV_SunColor
by pi and moved the 1/PI into the BRDF) and the raw local-light colours, so on
the scene-referred path every lit particle has been a constant pi - 1.65 stops -
brighter than the geometry around it. What that looks like is smoke, dust and fog
cards that are washed out and flat and do not sit in the scene.

One factor, on the diffuse lobe only. The emissive term in the same expression
does NOT take it: emittance is a radiance the material authored, not light
reflected off a surface, and it keeps the single exposure multiply it already
gets further down the shader. The environment-probe contribution is a separate
accumulator and is likewise untouched - probes were excluded from the BRDF factor
in S2 on purpose. SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR is exactly 1.0 off the switch.

research/s8-particles-rain-lensoptics.md 1.3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A72MFkdSczncE7au9UVnmu
---
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/LightVolumes.cfi | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/LightVolumes.cfi b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/LightVolumes.cfi
index d0eba3c4..1f07ac82 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/LightVolumes.cfi
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/LightVolumes.cfi
@@ -117,5 +117,18 @@ void ProjectLightVolume(in float3 vWorldPos, in half sunShadow, in half backLigh
 half3 GetEnvLighting(SParticleLightInfo lightInfo, half3 vNormal, half diffuseTerm, half emissiveTerm, half backLighting)
 {
 	half3 cLight = lightInfo.cDirectional * (lightInfo.ambientMult + max(0, dot(lightInfo.vDirectional, vNormal) + backLighting));
-	return cLight * diffuseTerm + emissiveTerm;
+
+	// S8, research/s8-particles-rain-lensoptics.md 1.3. This is the one lit path in the tree that
+	// the S2 pi audit missed, because it does not call anything named *BRDF: particles have their
+	// own light list and their own evaluation, and this line is their diffuse lobe. Its inputs are
+	// the radiometric sun (CV_SunColor, which S2 stopped dividing by pi) and the raw local-light
+	// colours, so without the normalisation factor every lit particle is pi - 1.65 stops - hotter
+	// than the geometry it sits against. What that looks like is smoke, dust and fog cards that
+	// are washed out and flat and do not sit in the scene.
+	//
+	// The particle SPECULAR lobe already supplies this factor explicitly (Particles.cfi,
+	// BlinnBRDF), and the emissive term below must NOT take it: emittance is a radiance the
+	// material authored, not light reflected off a surface, and it is exposed exactly once
+	// further down the shader. SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR is exactly 1.0 off the switch.
+	return cLight * (diffuseTerm * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR) + emissiveTerm;
 }
